        "original_id": "b0af1312-8e7b-593f-90fe-f0bc40085912",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johan Henrik Deuntzer\n- Organizations: Liberal \"Venstre\" party, Danish Social Liberal Party, Venstre Reform Party\n- Places: Denmark\n- Roles: politician, Council President\n- Events: 1901 Danish Folketing election\n- Governments: Cabinet of Deuntzer, Denmark's first liberal government\n\nFacts:\n- Johan Henrik Deuntzer was born on 20 May 1845 and died on 16 November 1918.\n- Johan Henrik Deuntzer was a Danish politician.\n- After the 1901 Danish Folketing election, Council President Johan Henrik Deuntzer of the Venstre Reform Party became the leader of Denmark's first liberal government.\n- Until 1905, Johan Henrik Deuntzer was a member of the Liberal \"Venstre\" party.\n- In 1905, Johan Henrik Deuntzer joined the Danish Social Liberal Party.\n- The Danish Social Liberal Party, also called Radikale Venstre or Radical Left, is a social-liberal political party in Denmark.",
